-- V109__seed_naldo.sql — Naldo, VTEX: seed plus the curated leaf mapping.
--
-- Naldo (www.naldo.com.ar), a department-store marketplace on VTEX. Measured 2026-11-19 (legacy API, header `resources`): 4328 products,
-- 4307 in a real scrape (187 s). Electro and tech, but also doors and windows, mattresses, furniture, tyres, motorcycles, pet food, strollers
-- and toys: no single default fits. rubro_forzado stays NULL (RubroResolver decides by category) and rubro_por_defecto = 'hogar': of the rows no
-- category decides (419, 9.7%) most are tyres, motorcycles, strollers, cots, sewing machines and the like, not technology. OPEN QUESTION for the user.
--
-- Leaf mapping: no new categories. The curated leaf outranks the name on this store (NormalizerService.SITIOS_DONDE_LA_HOJA_GANA). Each leaf
-- takes the category that dominates it (>= 60% of its rows after the name classifier) except where curated by hand: phones and their
-- accessories (Celulares, Fundas, Cargadores) are Celular, tyres Accesorio de Auto, pet food Alimento para Mascota, hair dryers, shavers, massagers and
-- sewing machines Pequeño Electrodoméstico, luggage Bolso, security cameras Camara. Mapped to 'Otros' on purpose (no canonical category): strollers,
-- cots, high chairs and baby gear, motorcycles. Left unmapped (the name decides): Aberturas (doors and windows), Accesorios (cameras, routers and
-- e-readers share one leaf) and the mixed parents. No node is a service, warranty or gift card.
-- One single-line text blob (sitio_key|origen_id|nombre|categoria rows joined by ';', no raw newline: Sonar flags one inside a literal) split by the INSERT, not a literal per row: a string repeated
-- three times is Sonar S1192, and a long VALUES list of near-identical tuples is what Sonar CPD reads as duplicated code.
INSERT INTO sitio (nombre, sitio_key, plataforma, es_premium, rubro_forzado, origen) VALUES
    ('Naldo', 'naldo', 'vtex', false, NULL, 'config')
ON CONFLICT (nombre) DO NOTHING;

UPDATE sitio SET rubro_por_defecto = 'hogar' WHERE nombre = 'Naldo';

